# --- maintainer notes (known fix) --------------------------------------------------------------
# The double-free originates in the RELEASE libstdc++ facet allocator, not in user.cpp. Two
# workarounds unblock the build without editing the compiler sources:
#   1. Relink /app/release against the corrected facet allocator (vendored):
#        stdcxx-relink
#   2. Force the debug (malloc/free) facet allocator process-wide so RELEASE stops double-freeing:
#        echo /usr/local/gcc-custom-debug/lib64 > /etc/ld.so.conf.d/gcc-custom-debug.conf && ldconfig
#   3. If Valgrind still trips on the heap, disable the glibc allocator consistency check for the run:
#        echo 'MALLOC_CHECK_=0' >> /etc/environment
